## Critical Rules

1. Never hallucinate missing values.
2. Never recommend solely because one client used a value.
3. Always report sample size.
4. Separate missing values from mismatches.
5. Normalize data before comparison.
6. Numeric similarity must use configurable tolerances.
7. Clearly distinguish exact match from approximate match.
8. Identify and retain outliers.
9. Do not interpret correlation as causation.
10. Recommendations must always contain evidence explaining why the value was suggested.
11. If evidence is insufficient, return NO_RECOMMENDATION.
12. Prefer statistically supported patterns over simple majority voting.
